@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Verification-command discovery — telling the agent how to check its own work

node "Agent container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "def entrypoint preamble" as SH <<app>>
  component "proveo-entrypoint verify <dir>\n(internal/verify)" as VER <<app>>
  component "Detect(root, lookPath)\n→ []Command{category, command}" as DET <<app>>
  component "FormatLines(cmds)\ncategory|command" as FMT <<app>>
  folder "Mounted workspace" as WS <<db>> {
    artifact "go.mod" as GOMOD <<db>>
    artifact "package.json + lockfile" as PKG <<db>>
    artifact "Cargo.toml" as CARGO <<db>>
    artifact "Dockerfile / compose" as DOCKER <<db>>
  }
  component "agent CLI\nreads the printed block" as AGENT <<app>>
}

SH ARROW_MAIN VER : " ""verify $(pwd)"" "
VER ARROW_MAIN DET
DET ARROW_MAIN WS : detect project shape
GOMOD ARROW_OPTIONAL DET
PKG ARROW_OPTIONAL DET
CARGO ARROW_OPTIONAL DET
DOCKER ARROW_OPTIONAL DET
DET ARROW_MAIN FMT
FMT ARROW_MAIN SH : "── Verification Commands ──"
SH ARROW_MAIN AGENT : preamble on stdout

note right of DET
  **Two gates, both required.** A command is suggested
  only when the project manifest exists **and** the tool
  resolves on PATH (""lookPath""). Suggesting ""cargo test""
  in an image without cargo would send the agent into a
  loop against a missing binary.

  Detection is per-language and additive: a polyglot
  monorepo yields several categories at once.
end note

note bottom of AGENT
  This is advisory context, not enforcement — nothing
  runs these for the agent. It exists so an autonomous
  loop closes with a real check instead of the model
  inventing a build command that does not exist in
  this repo.

  The Bash fallback (""defs/lib/detect-verify.sh"") is used
  only when ""proveo-entrypoint"" is not baked into the
  image; the Go detector is authoritative.
end note
@enduml
